WEBVTT

00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:15,020
I'm curious what you think of Ralph Moss's interview regarding soy. Do you still believe that soy

00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:21,420
is not beneficial for breast cancer patients after hearing this? He says the weaker estrogen of soy

00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:30,780
plugs the hole in the breast cancer cell so that the stronger bodily produced estrogen cannot get into

00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:40,140
the breast cell. Just curious if the genistine from soy that's an iso flavoid of soy will help

00:00:40,140 --> 00:00:49,500
lower my AFP or do you still advise me against it? So I think what he was looking at with this is

00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:58,460
fermented soy and he didn't state that in the interview and I think that was an error. I do think

00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:07,500
that soy iso flavoids are estrogen mimics and they should be avoided for people with any

00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:15,180
breast cancer even if you don't have ER positive or two positive or PR positive even if you're

00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:19,820
triple negative I still think you should still use soy. Now a good fermented soy is completely

00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:25,260
different fermented soy actually removes the estrogen from the estrogen beta receptor.

00:01:26,060 --> 00:01:34,140
So it is the attachment of the of the bad estrogen of the estrogen beta receptor that

00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:39,180
caused that blocks apoptosis. It's not about estrogen getting into the cell at all so

00:01:39,820 --> 00:01:48,220
his statement about that is not correct physiology. I think he's a great guy. I've interviewed him on my

00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:58,940
podcast before and but I don't think that's correct.

